{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqathh2z9c4","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Production retrieval is ungated: gate demoted to shadow scorer, bar is beat always inject","summary":"Strategic update (2026-06-12, user-confirmed): the gate as a retrieval FILTER never earned its place — every test showed its abstain hurt (gated iterative round 1 abstained and caused 0% on locale-sum; the fix made iterative round 1 ungated). Bench 3-arm design: on-search = best-case oracle (always retrieve+apply), on-iterative = PRODUCTION path with ungated round 1, off. No arm uses the gate inject verdict, and re-adding a gated arm would re-measure a characterized failure mode. Cost asymmetry: false abstain = catastrophic (0% solve), true abstain saves only 400-900 tokens — so any future gate (rule or learned) must show near-zero false negatives to beat ALWAYS-INJECT, the new deployment bar. Consequences: (1) gate becomes a SHADOW scorer — verdict computed and journaled on EVERY search (the as-shipped journal only fired on gated calls, the path production does not use; fix = move journaling above the ungated early-return, never enforce), giving clean would-it-have-helped data on real traffic; (2) the learned-model framing in [[note-mqasdxx0tnt]]/[[note-mqaslontp50]] shifts from better-filter to utility-predictor-in-shadow, enforcement only if data shows regions where abstain wins (interval-merge is the only one observed); if none emerge, value moves to note RANKING not gating. (3) The gated-A/B prediction in [[note-mqatdpw232s]] is MOOT (no gated arm exists). Tension flagged, not yet resolved: note-mq7kljz739q (defensibility = abstain-by-default gate) is contradicted by this and pending user supersede decision.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T11:02:16.763Z","vec":[-0.05233091861009598,-0.003017282346263528,-0.03683421015739441,0.013925665058195591,-0.002659016055986285,0.00018391261983197182,-0.0010572412284091115,-0.057215478271245956,0.055224381387233734